# 💡 Optional: batch the per-TC re-fetch into one query

The label-mode re-fetch added in `findDirectLinkedTCs` issues one `tracker.getIssue(tc.key)` call per direct TC — O(N) API reads per bug-done-check tick. A Bug with many linked TCs multiplies the reads every SM cycle (label mode only; `'none'` keeps zero extra reads, which is correctly pinned).

A single batched search collapses it to one call and still returns full fields (Jira: no `fields` restriction ⇒ everything incl. labels; ADO: `adoSearchFields` always includes `System.Tags`):

```javascript
if (tracker.stageFallback() === 'label' && tcs.length > 0) {
    try {
        var keys = tcs.map(function (tc) { return tc.key; });
        var full = tracker.searchIssues('key in ("' + keys.join('", "') + '")', { maxResults: keys.length });
        var byKey = {};
        full.forEach(function (f) { byKey[f.key] = f; });
        return tcs.map(function (tc) { return byKey[tc.key] || tc; });
    } catch (e) {
        console.warn('Could not re-fetch linked TCs with full fields — falling back to the link stubs:', e);
    }
}
return tcs;
```

Strictly optional — the current per-TC form is correct, degrades safely, and is fully tested; bugs rarely carry enough direct TCs for this to matter.

